<title>SOUTH KOREA: Five Daewoo Group firms on strike.</title>
<headline>Five Daewoo Group firms on strike.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Motor Co, Daewoo Heavy Industries Ltd and three other affiliates of South Korea's Daewoo Group were on strike, a group union official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The official, who declined to be identified, added later that a sixth Daewoo unit was also on strike. There are 15 unions at Daewoo Group of companies.</p>
<p>The strikes affected a total of 27,650 union workers, the official said.</p>
<p>&quot;These companies are on strike,&quot; he said, naming Daewoo Motor, Daewoo Heavy and its shipbuilding unit, Daewoo Precision Industries Ltd, Daewoo Automotive Components, and Daewoo Car Sales.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
